Subject: Program name "tar" on OpenVMS

On VMS argv[0] is the image's full file name, so messages read
"/DKA800/USERS/X/TAR.EXE: in: Cannot stat" and --help said "Usage:
TAR.EXE".  On VMS, replace argv[0] with getprogname () (patch 0002:
the image name in lower case) before set_program_name and argp see it.

--- a/src/tar.c
+++ b/src/tar.c
@@ -2754,6 +2754,12 @@
 main (int argc, char **argv)
 {
   set_start_time ();
+#ifdef __VMS
+  /* argv[0] is the image's full name ("/DKA0/GNU/BIN/TAR.EXE"), which
+     would head every message and the usage line; getprogname (patch 0002)
+     gives "tar".  */
+  argv[0] = (char *) getprogname ();
+#endif
   set_program_name (argv[0]);
 #ifdef ENABLE_ERROR_PRINT_PROGNAME
   error_print_progname = tar_print_progname;
